    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Marine hydrodynamics",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "In order to study the motion of marine structures and vessels, we need to understand the effects the surrounding fluid has on them.",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "This requires some basic concepts of hydrodynamics—which is fluid dynamics under special-case simplifications and assumptions particular of marine applications.",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "To solve problems related to ship motion we, need to know two things about the fluid:",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- velocity",
            "- pressure"
        ],
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Fluid flow description",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The velocity of the fluid at the location",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "**x**",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "**v**(**x**,t)",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "is given by the fluid-flow velocity vector:",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "this vector is usually described relative to an inertial coordinate system with origin in the mean free surface (h-frame, or s-frame).",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Incompressible fluid",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "For the flow velocities involved in ship motion, the fluid can be considered *incompressible*, *i.e.,* constant density.",
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Under this assumption, the net volume rate at a volume V enclosed by a surface *S* is",
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "since this is valid for all the regions V in the fluid, then by assuming that            is continuous, we obtain the",
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "*continuity equation* for incompressible flows:",
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Material derivative",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 4
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Let                      be a scalar function and                    a vector-valued function; then,",
        "page_idx": 4
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "If these are taken for the function",
        "page_idx": 4
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "then we have a special notation—material derivative:",
        "page_idx": 4
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/0da50ffa3fc24b00e84b300582c54e8bf25c27d5634ac8da442b202fb0eabba2.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 4
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
