    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Regular wave formulae (Faltinsen, 1990)",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 19
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/4dd231219a38fa66fb4e5b630e1c8cc5e432f7c12d026f85065ceff12bd715a0.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 19
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 19
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 19
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 19
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 19
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Potential theory for ships in waves",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 20
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The fluid forces are due to variations in pressure on the surface of the hull.",
        "page_idx": 20
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "It is normally assumed that the forces (pressure) can be made of different components",
        "page_idx": 20
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/0ca777aa4eafd1e0bbda804c28ef032a87ec388a647e6230c54b6afc419be169.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 20
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 20
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 20
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 20
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 20
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Potential theory for ships in waves",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 21
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Under linearity assumptions, the hydrodynamic problem is dealt as 2 separate problems and the solutions then added:",
        "page_idx": 21
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- Radiation problem: the ship is forced to oscillate in calm water."
        ],
        "page_idx": 21
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- Diffraction problem: the ship is restrained from moving in the presence of a wave field."
        ],
        "page_idx": 21
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Potentials:",
        "page_idx": 21
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "$\\Phi _{Total}=\\underbrace{\\sum_{}^{}\\Phi _{j}}_{Radiation problem}+\\underbrace{\\Phi _{Incident}+\\Phi _{Scattering}}_{Diffraction problem}$",
        "page_idx": 21
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "$\\Phi _{j}$",
        "page_idx": 21
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "\\- due to the motion in the j-th DOF.",
        "page_idx": 21
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 21
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 21
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 21
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 21
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Radiation potential",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 22
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Boundary conditions:",
        "page_idx": 22
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "free surface condition (dynamic+kinematic conditions)",
        "page_idx": 22
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "sea bed condition",
        "page_idx": 22
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "dynamic body condition",
        "page_idx": 22
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "radiation condition",
        "page_idx": 22
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "$\\Phi _{rad}=\\sum_{}^{}\\Phi _{j}$",
        "page_idx": 22
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "$\\nabla ^{2}\\Phi _{rad}=0$",
        "page_idx": 22
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 22
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 22
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 22
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 22
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Computing forces",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 23
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Forces and moments are obtained by integrating the pressure over the average wetted surface *Sw*:",
        "page_idx": 23
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Notation: i-th component",
        "page_idx": 23
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Radiation forces and moments:",
        "page_idx": 23
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "DOF:",
        "page_idx": 23
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "1-surge",
        "page_idx": 23
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "2-sway",
        "page_idx": 23
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "3-heave",
        "page_idx": 23
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "4-roll",
        "page_idx": 23
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "5-pitch",
        "page_idx": 23
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "6-yaw",
        "page_idx": 23
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Excitation forces (due to incident and scattered potentials) and moments:",
        "page_idx": 23
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 23
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 23
